# Incident catalog

**Impact: HIGH**

Non-obvious break/fix cases live in `.cursor/skills/gotchas/catalog.md`, not in this rule.

When the task matches a past failure (auth, Supabase keys, middleware, logged-in-only slowness, silent hangs):

1. **MUST** read that catalog before changing the same area.
2. Follow the invariant in the matching entry.

After fixing a surprising production or local failure (no useful error, only showed up when logged in, env/key/SDK mismatch, gateway timeout):

- **MUST** append a short entry to the catalog. Use the template in `.cursor/skills/gotchas/SKILL.md`.
- Do not turn the story into a new always-on rule. Keep this pointer short.
